<!--Post: 9960--><!--Time: 1109713702-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9960"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 1:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On Feb. 11, 1977, Gail Sorenson disappeared, abducted from a Dillon’s Store in downtown Hutchinson. <BR> <BR>“She was found two days later on the Arkansas River,” said Reno County Sheriff Randy Henderson. <BR> <BR>Henderson says the case bears striking similarities to two Sedgwick County cold cases now definitively linked to BTK. <BR> <BR>“One of the cases that Sheriff Steed discussed, one of the ladies had been kidnapped, found by a river,” Henderson said. “That enhanced my curiosity.” <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9960-->
<!--Post: 10043--><!--Time: 1109734929-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10043"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 7:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iq - that story was just on Fox news. Her body was not only dumped on the Arkansas River, but it was across the river from an LE shooting range!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10043-->
<!--Post: 10064--><!--Time: 1109738870-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10064"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it possible that he was on a training trip there? Maybe, a trip with boy scouts, or even a family trip, or a convention with ADT Security? What do ya think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10064-->
<!--Post: 10116--><!--Time: 1109770709-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10116"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 5:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The boy scout trip is a possibility, as that range is near a launching spot for canoeing trips.  When the river has enough water &#40;which it would have had in 77, before a resevoir upstream blocked much of the water&#41;, many groups would launch at Hutchinson and canoe all the way into Wichita.   <BR>However, that area is right along US HWY 50, so it may merely have been a convenient dumping spot in a town where he may have been unfamiliar with his surroundings.  The place where Sorenson was dumped has quite a few trees around it, and he may not have even known the range was there, as it is partily hidden.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10116-->
<!--Post: 10704--><!--Time: 1110144741-->
